# Project: Local AI VTuber Companion

## Goal
An AI VTuber companion with a local LLM for chat generation and ElevenLabs for TTS. Avatar/lipsync rendering is out of scope for now (see TBD).

## Stack decisions (already made, do not re-litigate unless there's a real problem)
- **Chat generation**: local LLM via Ollama (OpenAI-compatible API at `http://localhost:11434`), model `hf.co/HauhauCS/Qwen3.5-4B-Uncensored-HauhauCS-Aggressive:Q6_K` (switched from the 9B Gemma model — the 9B model alone used ~10GB/16GB VRAM, leaving too little headroom for faster-whisper's CUDA/cuBLAS init alongside it; under investigation as the cause of intermittent `cublas64_12.dll is not found or cannot be loaded` crashes in the voice harness / `speechToText.py`)
- **TTS**: ElevenLabs REST `text-to-speech` in `server/elevenlabs_tts.py` (Shiori replies only). Env: `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY`, `ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID` in `server/.env`. MP3 is base64-broadcast on the chat WS (`type: audio`) and played in the React client. Streaming websocket TTS is a future upgrade.
- **Bridge**: custom orchestrator server (Python) that clients connect to via WebSocket. This was chosen over a simpler folder-watch approach specifically because the connection needs to carry more than just audio later (expressions, status, interrupts, eventual STT).
- **STT**: `faster-whisper`, model `large-v3-turbo`, `device="cuda"`, `compute_type="float16"`. Turn-taking (deciding when an utterance starts/stops) is handled by a simple RMS energy-threshold VAD rather than a native VAD library — `webrtcvad` has no Python 3.14 wheels and is unmaintained, so a dependency-free heuristic was chosen instead.
- **Chat memory (Supabase)**: four-tier schema already live — `key_facts`, `rolling_summary`, `chat_memory` (`vector(768)` + HNSW), `recent_turns`, plus RPC `match_memory`. Embeddings via local Ollama `nomic-embed-text` (768-d). API in `chat_memory.py` (`store_turn`, `should_retrieve_memory`, `build_light_context` / `build_full_context`, `build_context_if_needed`, `prune_recent_turns`, etc.). Selective retrieval: heuristic gate skips semantic search on filler/chatty turns; light context = facts + summary (session-cached) + recent turns; full context adds `retrieve_relevant`. Wired into `voice_chat.py`: `build_context_if_needed` each turn (logs `(memory: light|full)`), turns stored after each reply, prune every 10 assistant turns (invalidates light cache). Env: `SUPABASE_URL` (project root, no `/rest/v1`), `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`.

## Architecture
[Text/Voice input] → orchestrator.py → Ollama (local LLM) → text reply
↓
ElevenLabs TTS API → audio bytes
↓
WebSocket broadcast (chat UI bridge, localhost:8766)
↓
React client (VN textbox + MP3 playback)

## Message protocol (WebSocket, JSON)
Chat UI bridge (live, localhost:8766 via `server/chat_bridge.py`, started by `voice_chat.py`):
```json
{"type": "chat", "who": "you", "text": "..."}
{"type": "chat", "who": "shiori", "text": "..."}
{"type": "audio", "format": "mp3", "data": "<base64>"}
{"type": "status", "value": "listening"}
{"type": "status", "value": "thinking"}
{"type": "status", "value": "speaking"}
{"type": "status", "value": "ready"}
{"type": "status", "value": "error", "detail": "..."}
```
The Vite client proxies `/ws` → `ws://127.0.0.1:8766`, live-replaces the VN textbox on each `chat` event, and plays `audio` MP3 for Shiori. Mic/STT remain in Python; TTS runs server-side before the Shiori `chat`+`audio` emit.

Every future feature should be a new `type` value, not a new connection or transport.

## Known unresolved items / caveats
- ElevenLabs streaming websocket endpoint has not been integrated yet; current path uses full-clip REST TTS (`elevenlabs_tts.py`) then WS `audio` to the UI.
- The mic-to-LLM test harness is split across `server/voice_chat.py` (entry/loop), `speechToText.py`, `local_model.py`, `elevenlabs_tts.py`, and `chat_bridge.py` (WS :8766 to the React UI). It is not yet wired into `orchestrator.py`.
- `key_facts` are read by light/full context builders but not auto-written yet (manual / future extractor).

## Environment notes
- Local GPU: RTX 5070 Ti, 16GB VRAM, used for local LLM inference via Ollama
- Windows desktop

## Immediate next step
Continue hardening the voice harness + chat UI path (STT → LLM → TTS → WS :8766), and wire it into `orchestrator.py` when ready.

